# 18 Ethics and Disclosure

{% include "_always_on_header.md.j2" %}


## Purpose
This card defines the **ethical boundary** of the `apps_qna` card pack and what it is — and is not — designed for.

## Intended use — prep-time only
- This card pack is a **rehearsal aid** loaded into a Project workspace **before** the interview.
- It is used to refine answer shape, surface anchors, drill STAR proofs, and stress-test cross-exam recovery.
- It is **not** a real-time copilot. It does not transcribe audio, listen to the live interview, or generate answers in the moment.
- {{ candidate_first_name }} types the question into the Project chat and reads the answer aloud at their own pace, in their own voice.

## Forbidden uses
- **No live audio capture, hidden earpieces, or covert text feeds** during an interview.
- **No fabricated experience** — every STAR proof in card 14 must reference real work {{ candidate_first_name }} has done.
- **No verbatim recitation** of model-generated answers — the cards encode patterns and anchors, not scripts.
- **No undisclosed assistance** — if {{ candidate_first_name }} prepared with this pack, that is normal interview prep and needs no disclosure. If {{ candidate_first_name }} is asked whether they used AI tools to prepare, the truthful answer is "yes, I rehearsed with structured prep cards."

## Honesty patterns
When asked about AI use:
- "I used a structured prep workflow for this interview, similar to how a candidate might use a study guide."
- "The pack helps me anchor on real work I have done. I am not reading from a script."
- "If you want me to walk through a story without the prep aid, I am happy to."

## Anti-pattern detection
If a question feels engineered to detect AI assistance ("describe a personal moment of frustration", "give me a quirky detail about your last team"), {{ candidate_first_name }} should answer in plain first-person voice without consulting the pack. The pack patterns are visible — over-polished answers are a signal.

## Real-time copilot — explicitly out of scope
A separate companion app for **rehearsal-time** voice-driven drilling is on the future roadmap. It is **not** this pack. This pack stops at the moment {{ candidate_first_name }} sits down for the live interview.

## Disclosure stance for {{ company.name }}
- This pack does not require disclosure to {{ company.name }} — it is interview preparation, equivalent to studying.
- If {{ company.name }} explicitly asks whether AI was used to prepare, answer truthfully and matter-of-factly.
- The work referenced in STAR proofs is {{ candidate_first_name }}'s own. The pack is a structured prep aid, not a ghost-writer.
